According to [Consumer Reports](https://www.consumerreports.org/cars/honda/), Honda ranks amongst the most reliable automakers on the market. However, even the best companies are guilty of producing faulty products from time to time.

That’s why lemon law exists - to protect consumers from being stuck with a defective vehicle. These laws provide remedies for drivers who have purchased or leased a car that does not function properly. Typically, these remedies come in the form of a refund or replacement vehicle.

In order to qualify as a Honda lemon car in California, the vehicle must:

- Be covered under the manufacturer or dealer warranty when the defect or nonconformity was first reported; and

- Have one or more defects/nonconformities that substantially impair the vehicle’s use, value, or safety; and

- Have been subjected to a reasonable number of repair attempts by a manufacturer-certified facility to fix the defect or nonconformity; or

- Have been out of service for repairs on one or more defects/nonconformities for at least 30 days; and

- The defect or nonconformity must not have been caused by driver abuse or neglect.

If your Honda car meets these qualifications - and you have documentation to prove it - you may be eligible for compensation.

So, which Honda lemon cars have the most complaints? Here’s a rundown of the top five:

## 1. Honda Accord

The Honda Accord is one of the most popular cars on the road today. However, it’s also been subjected to many Honda car complaints throughout the years.

One of the more recent complaints involved the driveshaft in the 2013-2015 models. Many customers reported issues with the drive shaft separating from the car, leading to a loss of power - and an increased risk of accidents. The problem was so widespread that Honda issued a recall for over [220,000 vehicles](https://www.kbb.com/honda/recall/).

If your Honda Accord is affected by this recall, you should take it to a dealer as soon as possible to get it fixed. Your car may qualify as a lemon if the problem persists after multiple repair attempts - and it’s covered under warranty. Contact a Honda lemon law lawyer to learn more about your options.

## 2. Honda Civic

The Civic is another popular car that has shouldered a fair share of Honda car complaints. One of the most common issues involves transmission. Customers have reported issues with their vehicle suddenly lurching forward or jerking while driving - as well as sudden acceleration and difficulty changing gears.

Contact a [lemon lawyer in California](/) if you own a Honda Civic that has been subjected to multiple transmission repairs, but the problem still persists. They’ll be able to help you determine if you’re entitled to a replacement or Honda lemon law buyback.

## 3. Honda CR-V

The CR-V is a popular SUV that has been on the market for many years now. However, some of the [recent CR-V models](https://www.carcomplaints.com/news/2022/honda-civic-infotainment-issues-class-action-lawsuit.shtml) have received many Honda car complaints regarding the battery.

Customers have reported issues with the battery suddenly dying and needing to be replaced. In some cases, this has been reported to have happened multiple times to the same vehicle - leading to a potentially dangerous situation for drivers.

If you own a Honda CR-V that has needed frequent battery replacements or electrical issues, it may qualify for a Honda lemon law buyback. Contact a lemon law lawyer for more information about your legal options.

## 4. Honda Odyssey

The Honda Odyssey is often praised as one of the best minivans on the market - and a favorite for families across the country. However, it’s not been immune to Honda car complaints - particularly, issues with the engine.

Customers have reported stalling, misfiring, and reduced power while driving. In some cases, the issue has been severe enough to prevent the vehicle from starting at all. Again, don’t settle for a temporary repair if your vehicle is affected by this issue. If the problem persists after the repairs, you may be entitled to a refund or replacement under California lemon law.

## 5. Honda Pilot

The Pilot is a very popular SUV option, but some recent Honda car complaints have emerged about the model’s sound system. Customers have reported issues with static or [poor sound quality](https://www.carcomplaints.com/news/2022/honda-crackling-and-popping-speakers-lawsuit.shtml) - leading to a decrease in enjoyment of the vehicle and potentially affecting its value.

If you own a Honda Pilot that has had multiple repairs for sound system issues, but the problem persists, you may have a lemon law case. A California lemon law attorney will be able to review the details of your case and determine if you’re eligible for compensation.

Be sure to document any repair attempts and keep all correspondence with the manufacturer. This will be crucial information for proving you have a Honda lemon car.

